  "limitations": [
    "Positive HOSTS genus overlap is only a possible taxonomic overlap between a commodity genus and a larval-host genus in a modern database, not the species shipped on a particular original voyage.",
    "Historic plant commodities can be processed or non-viable; no dispersal/plant establishment/actual butterfly feeding evidence.",
    "Some genus names have changed or are synonyms; exact source spellings chosen to prevent aggressive false positive matching.",
    "The 239 focal butterfly genus-level inventory is a globally pooled host list, not an island and historical period-specific larval record.",
    "A positive category on a historical pair does not imply that any focal butterfly or host species was transported during that voyage.",
    "The original HOSTS genus taxonomy is not guaranteed to be taxonomically reconciled to current WCVP accepted species.",
    "The matching species universe is the globally pooled fixed239, not necessarily the actual butterfly species recorded on an island.",
    "Cargo commodity genus associations are source-informed hypotheses and cannot be treated as records of exact species cargo."
